# Data Model

> Master data model. **Additive-only** — see `constitution/conventions.md`. Never edit or delete an existing `##` entity section from here; only append new ones (via `.rsw/scripts/merge_master_doc.py` at the end of `/rsw-review`). A feature's own draft lives at `features/<slug>/data-model.md` until it's merged in.

Each entity is its own `##` section so the merge script can parse section boundaries. Keep this exact shape per entity:

```
## <EntityName>

**Feature:** <slug> · **Added:** <YYYY-MM-DD>

<one or two sentences of description>

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | UUID | primary key |
| ... | ... | ... |

​```mermaid
erDiagram
    ENTITY_NAME ||--o{ RELATED_ENTITY : "relationship label"
​```
```

- Omit the Mermaid block for an entity with no interesting relationships yet — add it later as an additive change (a new entity section that references it, or, for a genuine correction, a user-approved manual edit).
- The Mermaid block is one atomic unit at merge time — never partially merged.
- If a new entity looks like it should relate to an existing one, include both sides of the relationship in the *new* entity's diagram block (e.g. `EXISTING ||--o{ NEW : "..."`) rather than editing the existing entity's section.

